          "definition": "Contexts $x_t$ are i.i.d. from an unknown distribution $P$. The finite action set $\\mathcal A$ and feature map $\\phi$ are public. The fixed unknown parameter and features lie in the Euclidean unit ball: $$\\|\\phi(x,a)\\|_2\\le1,\\quad\\|\\theta_\\star\\|_2\\le1,\\quad Y_t\\in[-1,1],\\quad\\mathbb E[Y_t\\mid x_t,a_t,\\mathcal H_{t-1}]=\\langle\\phi(x_t,a_t),\\theta_\\star\\rangle.$$ Rewards are fresh draws from the current conditional law. The learner observes the context, selects an action, and then receives that action's reward. $$d_{\\mathcal A}=\\max_x\\dim\\operatorname{span}\\{\\phi(x,a):a\\in\\mathcal A\\}\\le\\min\\{d,|\\mathcal A|\\}.$$"
